-- title:
--   The Čech complex of free abelian sheaves of a covering morphism is exact at the augmentation
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal C$ be a site with topology $J$ and finite wide pullbacks, in which abelian presheaves admit sheafification. Let $f:V\to U$ be a morphism such that the sieve generated by $f$ is a covering sieve of $U$. Write $\mathbb Z[T]$ for the free abelian sheaf on an object $T$. Then the sequence
--   $$\mathbb Z[V\times_U V] \xrightarrow{\;d_0\;} \mathbb Z[V] \xrightarrow{\;\mathbb Z[f]\;} \mathbb Z[U]$$
--   is exact (at $\mathbb Z[V]$), where $d_0$ is the first differential of the Čech complex of free abelian sheaves (the alternating sum of the two maps induced by the projections $V\times_U V\to V$) and the second map is the augmentation induced by $f$.
--
--   This is the low-degree part of the statement that the Čech complex of free abelian sheaves of a covering is a resolution, which is used to relate Čech and sheaf cohomology.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `C : Type (u + 1)` with `Category.{u}` and `[HasFiniteWidePullbacks C]`, `[HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}]`. The hypothesis is `Sieve.generate (Presieve.singleton f) ∈ J U`, and the conclusion is `.Exact` of the short complex `ShortComplex.mk (cechFreeD J f 0) (cechFreeAug J f) (cechFreeD_comp_aug J f)`. The augmentation `cechFreeAug J f` is the image under the free sheaf functor of the augmentation of the Čech nerve of `f` in degree $0$, i.e. of $f$ itself up to the identification of the $0$-th Čech term with $V$.
-- source:
--   B. Bhatt, P. Scholze, The pro-étale topology for schemes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1198 (v2, 17 Dec 2014). Lean source: idealson-nexources/proetale (fork of chrisflav/proetale by C. Merten, J. Jiang and contributors, Apache-2.0), commit 2983805, file Proetale/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Sites/SheafCohomology/CechResolution.lean, lines 592-613 (`CategoryTheory.cechFree_exact_zero`).

